  "caption": "Kilometre 18 of Quinn's first half marathon: the hamstring locked mid-stride. Three bottles of water later, still cramping.\n\nExercise cramps are often driven by muscle fatigue, working beyond what those muscles are trained for, rather than dehydration alone. Salt or bananas alone are unlikely to prevent them.\n\nWhat can help: train for the distance and intensity that brings on cramps, strengthen the muscles that tend to cramp, pace the early part of a session, and for heavy sweaters in the heat, fluids plus electrolytes can be part of the plan. If a cramp hits, ease off and stretch gently.\n\nGet it checked if cramps happen at rest, come with weakness, numbness or swelling, or a calf stays painful.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
